      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 51 year-old man with a renal cancer (pT3N0M0) consulted at the emergency department for persistent headache initiated a week before and recent vomiting. Physical examination and blood analyses were not remarkable. Cerebral magnetic resonance imaging demonstrated radiological signs of meningitis. The differential diagnosis of meningitis is discussed."},
